<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113946" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθές</span></b> , Adv. (lengthd. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθές</span></b>  (q.v.); where the word
		occurs in <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>NT,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Jo.
				4.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				7.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
				13.8
			</span></i>, codd. vary betw. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθές</span>
			and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθές; χθές</span> is not found in
			Ptolemaic papyri, but in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				2.161.8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>):—<i>yesterday,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Merc.
				273
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.113
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				327a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Smp.</u>
				174a
			</span></i>, etc.: freq. placed between Art. and Subst.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ χ. ὁμολογία, οἱ χ. λόγοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				216a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ti.</u>
				26e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ χ. ἡμέρᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.773e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. μὲν . . , τὰ νῦν δὲ</span> .
			. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				17a
			</span></i>: freq. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρώην τε καὶ χ., χ. καὶ
				πρώην,</span>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρώην</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. καὶ τρίτην ἡμέραν</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.3.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				31.2
			</span></i>. (Cf. Skt. <i>hyás</i> 'yesterday', Lat.
				<i>heri, hesternus,</i> OHG. <i>gestaron</i> 'yesterday',
			etc.)</div>
